# Pairs with TypeOK. The close's bound on the bump is dropped, so a close at the
# top of the generation domain bumps past it. The bound stands for the finite
# generations of the model; the mutation checks that the domain bound is real.
MODULE: TypeOkCloseUnbounded
TARGET: TypeOK
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the close bumps the generation with no room check and leaves the generation domain
PERTURBS: Close

--- FIND
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
    /\ fEpoch < MaxEpoch
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
    /\ hoOpen
    /\ ~closing
\* MUTATION: no bound on the bump.
    /\ fAdmit' = FALSE
--- END
